      "content": "\"bypassing conscious skepticism\"... that's exactly what I'm talking about. it doesn't feel like they're just trying to look \"trustworthy,\" it feels like they're trying to hijack a specific part of my brain. \n\nif they're using these patterns to \"outweigh rational doubts,\" isn't that basically a form of neuro-linguistic programming? like, if you look at the way the cobalt blue fades into those sharp, angular lines in the latest print ad, it's almost like a visual trigger. can you look at the actual geometric structure of that pattern and tell me if it could actually be used as a subconscious command? like, is there a mathematical way these shapes could be designed to force a specific cognitive response?",
